course: dictionary
lesson: 585
title: Automatic: working by itself
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Automatic means working by itself, without a person deciding each step. «The automatic doors opened as we walked up.» Nobody pushed them. A sensor noticed us and the door moved on its own.
explain: Some automatic things happen without thinking, like blinking or your knee jerking when a doctor taps it. These quick automatic movements are called reflexes. «A reflex is a quick automatic movement.»
explain: Automatic can also mean certain to happen because of a rule. «Breaking this rule means an automatic red card.» Look at the clue words in the sentence to see whether a machine, a body, or a rule is in charge.
fact: Automatic means working by itself, without a person controlling each step.
fact: An automatic action is done without thinking, from habit or reflex.
fact: Automatic can also mean certain to happen because of a rule.
fact: An automatic is a car with automatic gears.
fact: «An automatic door uses a motion sensor to notice movement.»
exercise: «The automatic doors opened as we walked up.» What made the doors open? | They were always open | *A sensor noticed us and the door moved by itself | A person pushed them | The wind blew them open
exercise: Blinking your eyes is an automatic action. What does automatic mean here? | Done only on Sundays | Done by a teacher | *Done without thinking | Done very slowly with great care
exercise: «Breaking this rule means an automatic red card.» What does automatic mean in this sentence? | Done by a machine | Happening very slowly | Sometimes, if the referee feels like it | *Certain to happen because of the rule
test: Practice makes your times tables ___, so you can answer without counting. | Noisy | Gentle | Careful | *Automatic
test: Which one is an automatic machine? | A pencil | A bag of sugar | *An automatic washing machine | A bicycle you pedal yourself
exam: «Automatic captions guess words from sound and sometimes mishear.» What does automatic mean in this sentence? | Typed slowly by a person | *Done by a computer by itself, without a person typing each word | Always correct and perfect | Written in capital letters
